{"test": "A2_t2_trivial_bundle", "first_levels": [{"lam": 0.0, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 1.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 2.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 4.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 5.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 8.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 9.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 10.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 13.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 16.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 17.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 18.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 20.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 25.0, "mult": 12}, {"lam": 26.0, "mult": 8}], "additivity_check_pass": true, "verdict": "Trivial T\u00b2 = S\u00b9 \u00d7 S\u00b9 Laplacian spectrum is exact additive sum \u03bb_{n,m} = n\u00b2 + m\u00b2 with multiplicities multiplying. The trivial-bundle additivity is the 1D analog of Spike #7's S\u00b2 + U(1) \u2192 S\u00b3 identity, BUT here the bundle is trivial (c1 = 0 trivially since base is 1D) so the 'fibre' is just a direct product. No non-trivial encoding channel."}
{"test": "A3_t2_twisted_bundle", "omega_sweep": [{"omega": 0.0, "first_levels": [{"lam": 0.0, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 1.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 2.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 4.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 5.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 8.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 9.0, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 10.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 13.0, "mult": 8}, {"lam": 16.0, "mult": 4}], "ground_state_eigval": 0.0}, {"omega": 0.25, "first_levels": [{"lam": 0.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 0.5625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 1.0625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 1.5625, "mult": 3}, {"lam": 2.5625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 3.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 4.0625, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 4.5625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 5.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 5.5625, "mult": 2}], "ground_state_eigval": 0.0625}, {"omega": 0.5, "first_levels": [{"lam": 0.25, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 1.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 2.25, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 3.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 4.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 6.25, "mult": 6}, {"lam": 7.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 9.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 10.25, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 11.25, "mult": 4}], "ground_state_eigval": 0.25}, {"omega": 0.75, "first_levels": [{"lam": 0.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 0.5625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 1.0625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 1.5625, "mult": 3}, {"lam": 2.5625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 3.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 4.0625, "mult": 4}, {"lam": 4.5625, "mult": 2}, {"lam": 5.0625, "mult": 1}, {"lam": 5.5625, "mult": 2}], "ground_state_eigval": 0.0625}], "verdict": "Aharonov-Bohm-twisted T\u00b2 (S\u00b9 base, U(1) fibre, holonomy \u03c9) shifts m-eigenvalues to (m + \u03c9)\u00b2. Ground state eigenvalue grows monotonically from 0 (at \u03c9=0) to 0.25 (at \u03c9=1/2) as expected: \u03c9 = 1/2 maximises ground-state lift since m and -m become non-degenerate. \u03c9 \u2208 \u2124 is gauge-equivalent to \u03c9 = 0 (holonomy U(1)-valued mod integers). NON-TRIVIAL spectral content emerges from the gauge connection, even though the underlying bundle is topologically trivial as a manifold (T\u00b2 = S\u00b9 \u00d7 S\u00b9)."}
